# Documentation Update Walkthrough

## Overview

Successfully updated all project documentation to reflect the complete work history from project inception through version 2.2.0, including all implemented features, architectural decisions, and development principles.

---

## What Was Accomplished

### 1. Created Development Principles Document ✅

**New File**: [DEVELOPMENT_PRINCIPLES.md](file:///d:/Dev/antigravity/docs/DEVELOPMENT_PRINCIPLES.md)

This comprehensive guide documents the core development principles used throughout the project:

- **RAII (Resource Acquisition Is Initialization)** - How we manage FFmpeg, DirectX, and other C-style resources
- **Modular Design** - Component isolation and separation of concerns
- **Code Reusability** - Wrapping third-party libraries in clean C++ classes
- **Memory Safety** - Smart pointers, container safety, and thread safety patterns
- **Thread Safety & Concurrency** - Threading model with mutex protection and priority queues
- **Clean Room Code** - Documentation standards and code review checklist

**Purpose**: This document serves as a template for future projects, capturing the best practices developed during this project.

---

